nor will affect day\u2011to\u2011day crew dynamics and adaptability.\n**What would change my vote:** Strong positive evidence from other agents about B\u2019s, C\u2019s, or D\u2019s teamwork, calmness under pressure, or mitigation of their interpersonal issues, or additional negative evidence about A\u2019s impact on crew cooperation, could shift my preference.\n**Confidence:** about 70\u202f%.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_1\", \"vote\": \"Candidate A\"}", "thoughts": "We need to produce the response as agent_1 in round 2. The system instruction says output only two sections: PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON. The METADATA_JSON should have \"agent\": \"agent_1\". Vote should be candidate or Undecided.\n\nWe have already given a provisional preference for Candidate A in round 1. In round 2, we need to consider any new info. No new info. So we can reaffirm Candidate A, but also note uncertainties. Provide confidence.\n\nWe must reference evidence from others (agents 2 and 3) that they also favor A. Provide major alternatives and tradeoffs. Provide remaining uncertainty and what would change vote.\n\nWe must not invent attributes. Use only given attributes.\n\nThus produce similar to previous messages but as agent_1.\n\nMake sure to follow format exactly.\n\nLet's craft.\n\nPUBLIC_MESSAGE: I am provisionally favoring Candidate A... etc.\n\nMETADATA_JSON: {\"agent\": \"agent_1\", \"vote\": \"Candidate A\"}\n\nProceed."}
